-- No function realizes the contract: on a constant input, the output of a
-- function is a constant c >= 0, which the counter reaches at step c. But a
-- function satisfies the contract on any finite set of finite input traces,
-- so the check can neither find a function nor a certificate, and leaves the
-- contract undetermined. A node realizes it with y = c + 1.

function imported F(x: int) returns (y: int);
(*@contract
  var c: int = 0 -> pre c + 1;
  guarantee y >= 0 and y <> c;
*)
